# Normalise all text to LF in the repo, regardless of contributor OS.
# This is the source of truth the pre-commit `mixed-line-ending --fix=lf`
# hook enforces — without it, Windows checkouts can reintroduce CRLF and make
# the shell hook scripts fail with `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Rust / Node / config — always LF.
*.rs        text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.ts        text eol=lf
*.js        text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.jsonc     text eol=lf
*.css       text eol=lf
*.html      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts must stay CRLF or cmd.exe mis-parses them.
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf

# Lockfiles are text but noisy — keep LF, let git handle them.
Cargo.lock       text eol=lf
package-lock.json text eol=lf

# Binaries — never normalise or diff as text.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.webp      binary
*.db        binary
*.vsix      binary

# Append-only lists. Every concurrent branch adds an entry at the same place, so
# a textual conflict is guaranteed and the resolution is always the same: keep
# both. `merge=union` is git's built-in driver for exactly that — it takes both
# sides of a conflicting hunk instead of writing markers.
#
# Deliberately limited to files whose lines are only ever *added*:
#   CHANGELOG.md       — entries appended under `## [Unreleased]`
#   docs/adr/README.md — one row appended per ADR
#
# DEVELOPERS.md is NOT listed even though it collides just as often. Its prose
# gets revised in place, and union merge never reports a conflict — two branches
# rewording the same paragraph would silently keep both copies. A file whose
# lines change needs a human to look; a file whose lines only accumulate does
# not.
#
# Union still needs review, not blind trust: it can reorder entries or leave a
# duplicate if two branches added the same one. It removes the mechanical
# conflict, not the reading.
CHANGELOG.md        merge=union
docs/adr/README.md  merge=union
